{{Short description|1966 Football Tournament Group}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=February 2021}}
'''Group 3 of the [[1966 FIFA World Cup]]''' consisted of holders [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], [[Hungary national football team|Hungary]], [[Portugal national football team|Portugal]], and [[Bulgaria national football team|Bulgaria]]. Play began on 12 July 1966 and concluded on 20 July 1966. World Cup newcomers Portugal won the group, Hungary finished as runners-up, and both advanced to the quarter-finals. Meanwhile, Bulgaria and defending Champions Brazil failed to advance.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Stokkermans |first1=Karel |last2=Jarreta |first2=Sergio Henrique |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/66f.html |title=World Cup 1966 (England, July 11–30) |website=RSSSF.com |publisher=[[Rec.Sport.Soccer Statistics Foundation]] |date=22 October 1999 |access-date=26 May 2018}}</ref>

